# The posture checks known to fail on each form (make check; test/boot):
#
#   FORM ID...
#   ARCH ID...
#
# A form takes the * line, or, built with DEV=1 as make check builds every
# form, the dev line; a FORM line, and an ARCH line (x86_64, aarch64), add
# their ids to it, for that form and on that architecture. ?ID may fail
# or not, as the host decides. Each is a weakness still
# open (docs/security.md, "Not yet"): test/boot fails a machine on any
# other failure, and on any of these that starts passing, so this list
# cannot claim less, or more, than the machines hold.
#
# No form carries a shell but those that log people in (sshd, lima,
# prod-ssh) and DEV=1 builds, which add busybox-full: its shell, awk,
# wget, nc and telnetd. make check-dist boots prod-ssh's release disk as it
# ships: busybox for the logins sshd serves, and sshd listening.

dev network-no-login programs-no-downloaders programs-no-interpreters programs-no-shell
*
# qemu-host has KVM, as its form allows, wherever its host lends it the
# hardware: EL2 on aarch64 (Apple M3 and later, QEMU 11), VMX or SVM on
# x86_64.
qemu-host ?kernel-no-hypervisor
prod-ssh network-no-login programs-no-downloaders programs-no-interpreters programs-no-shell
